  "id": "multivariate-normal-distribution",
  "term": "multivariate normal distribution",
  "definition": "A multivariate normal distribution is a probability model for several continuous variables considered together. In this context, it is used as the assumed joint distribution for continuous multivariate data when building Gaussian graphical models.",
